## 4. Auth

Log in once per credential family in the setup project and persist `storageState`. Use `AUTH_FILE` for the primary family and `ALT_AUTH_FILE` for the second. Two-family flows open a second context with `browser.newContext({ storageState: ALT_AUTH_FILE })`. Read credentials from `process.env`; never log in inside every test.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
// playwright.config.ts — setup project writes AUTH_FILE / ALT_AUTH_FILE
test.use({ storageState: AUTH_FILE });

test("collaborator sees shared item @smoke", async ({ browser }) => {
  const owner = await browser.newContext({ storageState: AUTH_FILE });
  const collaborator = await browser.newContext({ storageState: ALT_AUTH_FILE });
  // ...
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto("/login");
  await page.getByLabel("Email").fill(process.env.E2E_USER_EMAIL!);
  await page.getByLabel("Password").fill(process.env.E2E_USER_PASSWORD!);
});
```

**Why:** Setup-time auth is fast and stable; per-test UI login multiplies flake and tempts hardcoded secrets.

