## 11. Assertions

Default to web-first `expect(locator)`. Use `expect.soft` when one scenario needs several independent checks. Use `toHaveScreenshot` only with dynamic regions masked.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
await expect.soft(card).toContainText("Due tomorrow");
await expect.soft(card.getByRole("link", { name: "Open" })).toBeVisible();
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot({ mask: [page.locator(".timestamp")] });
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
const text = await card.textContent();
expect(text).toContain("Due tomorrow");
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot(); // clock, avatars, ads unmasked
```

**Why:** Locator assertions auto-wait; soft asserts surface all failures; masked screenshots avoid cosmetic flake.

---

## 12. Anti-flake

Retries belong in CI configuration only—not as a local crutch. Keep tests isolated. Use `page.clock` when behavior depends on “now” (availability windows, calendars). Pin locale and timezone in config. Enable trace on first retry. Raising `retries: 5` or forcing `workers: 1` is not a substitute for fixing root cause.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
test("shows slot on booked day @regression", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.clock.install({ time: new Date("2026-01-15T10:00:00Z") });
  await page.goto("/schedule");
  await expect(page.getByRole("button", { name: "10:00 AM" })).toBeEnabled();
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
// playwright.config.ts
retries: 5,
workers: 1, // "fixes" every test
// spec: no clock; uses real today and hopes CI timezone matches laptop
```

**Why:** Isolation and controlled time remove race conditions; traces diagnose real failures instead of masking them with retries.

---

## Refusals (hard stops)

Never weaken or delete an assertion to pass. Never “heal” a real product bug—triage, then fix the app or open a defect. Never replace a role locator with CSS or XPath to unblock a test. Never use `waitForTimeout`, a hardcoded credential, or the `any` type. Each of these is a conflict the agent must raise; they are not preferences that can be negotiated away.
